  m_text: "generated and used within an organization. It helps identify which sources
    produce the most valuable information and how consistently that data is created.
    By analyzing patterns in data production, businesses can detect inefficiencies
    in the way information is collected. This allows them to improve data-generation
    processes and ensure higher accuracy and reliability. When organizations understand
    how their data is made, they can better prepare it for deeper analysis and decision-making.\n\n
    Data mining also guides the creation of new data by highlighting gaps or missing
    information needed for better insights. Companies often design new data-collection
    methods after discovering trends that require more detailed tracking. This results
    in richer datasets that support stronger predictive models and better business
    strategies. Through continuous analysis, data mining ensures that newly generated
    data remains relevant and aligned with organizational goals. Ultimately, it creates
    a cycle... "
